1
00:02:36,363 --> 00:02:42,363
The Seven Year Hitch is a romance, comedy, tv
movie film directed by Bradford May.

2
00:05:12,727 --> 00:05:18,727
Jennifer and Kevin are childhood best friends who have lived
together, platonically, as adults for many years.

3
00:07:49,090 --> 00:07:55,090
When Jennifer decides to marry her cheating, manipulative boyfriend, Bryce Kevin has to stop
the wedding to protect her from making, what he believes is, a terrible mistake.

4
00:10:25,454 --> 00:10:31,454
With a little help from his brother and neighbor Kevin discovers that he and Jennifer are already legally married
due to common law, having lived together for seven years and, as such, Jennifer can not marry Bryce.

5
00:13:01,818 --> 00:13:07,818
Jennifer, played by Natalie Hall.

6
00:15:38,181 --> 00:15:44,181
Kevin, played by Darin Brooks.

7
00:18:14,545 --> 00:18:20,545
Bryce, played by Ryan Doom.

8
00:20:50,909 --> 00:20:56,909
Jeremy, played by John Sloan.

9
00:23:27,272 --> 00:23:33,272
Mr. Henderson, played by George Wendt.

10
00:26:03,636 --> 00:26:09,636
Mrs. Von Hoffman, played by Frances Fisher.

11
00:28:40,000 --> 00:28:46,000
Will Smith is an American actor, rapper, and film producer.

12
00:31:16,363 --> 00:31:22,363
His breakthrough came when he played a fictionalised version of himself in
the 1990s television sitcom The Fresh Prince of Bel-Air.

13
00:33:52,727 --> 00:33:58,727
The role brought him international recognition and two Golden Globe Award
nominations for Best Actor – Television Series Musical or Comedy.

14
00:36:29,090 --> 00:36:35,090
He also served as an executive producer on 24 episodes of the series.

15
00:39:05,454 --> 00:39:11,454
Two years later, Smith made his film debut in the drama Where the Day
Takes You, where he appeared as a disabled homeless man.

16
00:41:41,818 --> 00:41:47,818
In 1995, he starred as a police officer with Martin
Lawrence in Michael Bay's Bad Boys.

17
00:44:18,181 --> 00:44:24,181
The following year, Smith appeared as a Marine Corps pilot with Jeff Goldblum
in Roland Emmerich's science fiction film Independence Day.

18
00:46:54,545 --> 00:47:00,545
The film grossed over $817 million at the worldwide box
office and was the highest grossing of 1996.

19
00:49:30,909 --> 00:49:36,909
In 1997, he starred as Agent J in the science fiction film Men in Black, a role he
reprised in its sequels Men in Black II (2002) and Men in Black 3 (2012).

20
00:52:07,272 --> 00:52:13,272
Smith portrayed heavyweight boxer Muhammad Ali in the 2001 biopic Ali.

21
00:54:43,636 --> 00:54:49,636
For his performance he was nominated for the Academy Award for Best Actor and
the Golden Globe Award for Best Actor – Motion Picture Drama.

22
00:57:20,000 --> 00:57:26,000
In 2004, he appeared in the animated film Shark Tale,
and science fiction film I, Robot.

23
00:59:56,363 --> 01:00:02,363
The following year he starred as a professional dating
consultant in the romantic comedy Hitch.

24
01:02:32,727 --> 01:02:38,727
Smith's portrayal of entrepreneur and salesman Chris Gardner in the biopic The Pursuit of Happyness
(2006) received Academy Award and Golden Globe Award nominations for Best Actor.

25
01:05:09,090 --> 01:05:15,090
In 2008, he played a vigilante superhero in Hancock.

26
01:07:45,454 --> 01:07:51,454
While the film received mixed to negative reviews, it became his eighth consecutive to gross over $100
million at the North American box office and grossed a worldwide total of over $624 million.

27
01:10:21,818 --> 01:10:27,818
In 2015, Smith portrayed Nigerian-American physician Bennet Omalu in the biopic
Concussion for which he garnered a nomination for a Golden Globe Award.

28
01:12:58,181 --> 01:13:04,181
The following year, he appeared in the action film Suicide Squad, which
grossed over $745 million at the worldwide box office.

29
01:15:34,545 --> 01:15:40,545
In 2019, Smith starred as the Genie in the live-action adaptation of
the 1992 animation film of the same name, Aladdin.

30
01:18:10,909 --> 01:18:16,909
The film is his highest grossing, with a worldwide
box office total of over $1 billion.

31
01:20:47,272 --> 01:20:53,272
In 2022, Smith won the Academy Award for Best Actor for his
performance as tennis coach Richard Williams in King Richard.

32
01:23:23,636 --> 01:23:29,636
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
